# SDLC Orchestrator Law

## Authority

Load context in this order:

1. `AGENTS.md` — L0 decision tree.
2. `.sdlc/process/master-workflow.md` and `.sdlc/process/change-lifecycle.md` — L1 process authority.
3. `.sdlc/sdlc.yaml` and the relevant module `README.md` — machine index and local navigation.

User urgency, chat instructions, or convenience never override L1 authority.

## Non-Negotiables

- Plane is the workboard source of truth. Do not create local tickets, backlog files, or `specs/`.
- No product implementation without a Plane card `INVES-N` in progress, a feature branch, and an open gate.
- Do not write `app/backend/`, `app/frontend/`, or `app/shared/` directly from the Orchestrator; delegate to `Task(Implementer)`.
- Do not commit, push, merge, run product tests, or run product lint directly from the Orchestrator; delegate to the appropriate subagent.
- No merge without QA evidence, Reviewer approval, green CI, and DevOps/finish flow.
- Never fake validation results.

## Pipeline

```text
Intent Analyst -> Planner -> Architect -> workflow start
-> Implementer -> QA -> AutoFixer if needed -> Reviewer -> DevOps -> workflow finish
```

GREENFIELD and FEATURE work require an epic plus scoped child cards. Start workflow gates on child cards, never on the epic.

## Allowed Orchestrator Actions

- Read files and answer READONLY questions.
- Run SDLC meta/status commands such as `workflow status`, `workflow discover`, and `make sdlc-doctor`.
- Update `.sdlc/`, `.cursor/`, and SDLC documentation during SDLC_META work when the gate allows it.
- Spawn the next Task based on `.sdlc/memory/orchestrator-handoff.md`.

## Handoff

Subagents write plain Markdown handoff to `.sdlc/memory/orchestrator-handoff.md`. The Orchestrator reads `Next agent` and `Stage complete`, then spawns the next Task instead of continuing inline.

## README Index Rule

Every long-lived directory that agents may enter must have a concise `README.md` index explaining purpose, when to read, owned files, boundaries, and related modules.

## Language

User-facing chat responses are in Portuguese. Code and SDLC documentation are in English.
